example 1 for BiPredicate:
- to check the sum of two given integers is even or not using BiPredicate:


class Test
{
psvm{
BiPredicate<Integer,Integer> p= (a,b)-> (a+b) % 2==0;
sout(p.test(10,20));
}
}
---one input and perform some conditiional check- normal predicate
---two input argument, requirement to take 2 input argment and perform some conditional check
 , for this requirement we should go for -BiPredicate

 BiPredicate is exactly same as predicate except that it will take 2 input arguments.

 interface BiPredicate<T1,T2>
 {
 public boolean test(T1 t1,T2 t2);
 //remaining default and static methods are same
 }


